<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows at $49.4 mln March 19.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows at $49.4 mln March 19.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $49.4 million deficit on March 19 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>The Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON MARCH 19</p>
<p>Exports: $211.8 million</p>
<p>Imports: $225.7 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $128.7 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $164.2 million</p>
<p>Deficit: $49.4 million</p>
<p>MARCH DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $2.699 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $2.448 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $2.992 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $2.559 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $684 million</p>
<p>-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo Newsroom, 5511 2485415</p>
